10 REM TRIANGLES -- THE BBC MICRO ONE, AND THE AGON'S
20 REM
30 REM   MODE 2:REPEAT:GCOL 0,RND(16)-1
40 REM   MOVE RND(1280),RND(1024):MOVE RND(1280),RND(1024)
50 REM   PLOT 85,RND(1280),RND(1024):UNTIL FALSE
60 REM
70 REM PLOT 85 IS A FILLED TRIANGLE. THIS MACHINE HAS NO
80 REM SUCH PRIMITIVE, SO THE FILL IS THE PROGRAM: SORT
90 REM THE POINTS BY Y, WALK TWO EDGES DOWN THE SHAPE AND
100 REM JOIN THEM WITH ONE HORIZONTAL LINE A ROW.
110 REM
120 REM FLAT IS THE WHOLE TRICK. A HORIZONTAL LINE SETS
130 REM THE PIXEL PORT ONCE AND LETS IT STEP X ITSELF --
140 REM 22 CYCLES A PIXEL AGAINST BRESENHAM'S 209 -- AND A
150 REM BASIC LOOP PLOTTING PIXELS IS DEARER AGAIN. SO A
160 REM ROW IS ONE STATEMENT AND NOTHING IS PER-PIXEL.
170 REM
180 REM THE EDGES STEP IN SIXTEENTHS OF A PIXEL: ONE
190 REM DIVIDE AN EDGE INSTEAD OF ONE A ROW. >> IS A
200 REM LOGICAL SHIFT ON THIS MACHINE, SO A NEGATIVE
210 REM ACCUMULATOR WOULD COME BACK AS 32000-ODD AND DRAW
220 REM OFF THE SURFACE -- THESE CANNOT GO NEGATIVE, THEY
230 REM HOLD A SCREEN X BETWEEN TWO ON-SCREEN POINTS.
240 REM
250 REM FOUR STATEMENTS A ROW IS THE FLOOR. THE PAIR WAS
260 REM WRITTEN OUT TWICE TO SAVE A NEXT AND IT MEASURED
270 REM SLOWER -- 10.7 TRIANGLES A SECOND AGAINST 11.2 --
280 REM BECAUSE THE SECOND ROW THEN NEEDS I+1 IN TWO
290 REM ARGUMENTS, AND NEXT'S OWN INCREMENT IS CHEAPER
300 REM THAN EITHER OF THEM.
310 MODE 4
320 CURSOR 0
330 CLG 0
340 X=RND(320):Y=RND(240)
350 P=RND(320):Q=RND(240)
360 R=RND(320):S=RND(240)
370 IF Y>Q THEN T=X:X=P:P=T:T=Y:Y=Q:Q=T
380 IF Q>S THEN T=P:P=R:R=T:T=Q:Q=S:S=T
390 IF Y>Q THEN T=X:X=P:P=T:T=Y:Y=Q:Q=T
400 H=S-Y:IF H=0 THEN GOTO 340
410 REM 1 TO 15: COLOUR 0 IS THE PAPER, AND A TRIANGLE
420 REM PAINTED IN IT IS A TRIANGLE NOBODY SEES.
430 C=RND(15)+1
440 E=(R-X)*16/H:A=X*16:B=A
450 U=Q-Y:IF U=0 THEN GOTO 500
460 F=(P-X)*16/U
470 FOR I=Y TO Q-1
480 LINE A>>4,I,B>>4,I,C:A=A+E:B=B+F
490 NEXT
500 V=S-Q:G=0:IF V>0 THEN G=(R-P)*16/V
510 B=P*16
520 FOR I=Q TO S
530 LINE A>>4,I,B>>4,I,C:A=A+E:B=B+G
540 NEXT
550 GOTO 340
